WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:05.500
In every market, a community gathers around a story. Sherwood Forest gives that story roots.

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:15.200
Start in the market grove. Every token shows its price, activity, ownership, and immutable reward basket before you trade.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:23.800
Choose the community you believe in, inspect the assets its market can grow, and enter with a bounded quote you can verify before signing.

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:36.900
When this Devnet trade confirms, ownership updates onchain. The transaction succeeds on its own terms. Then, as a best-effort second step, the protocol advances one piece of that token's maintenance work.

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:50.000
Every fee is assigned before anything external happens. Fifty percent belongs to holder baskets. Twenty-five percent belongs to the creator. Twenty percent flows to eligible RDAO stakers. Five percent belongs to the governed treasury.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:01:00.500
A delayed conversion cannot silently change those shares. As activity continues, each healthy basket leg converts independently.

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:13.300
Purchased assets are held for that launch and streamed to eligible holders. Claims pull already-accounted rewards from custody; they do not sell the token and buy the basket at withdrawal.

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:30.100
Creators begin with one guided launch. Name the token, publish its media and links, and choose up to three supported reward assets. Supply, basket weights, fee rules, and creator identity take root together. There is no hidden creator token allocation.

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:44.000
The market begins on a transparent bonding curve. When it graduates, reserved tokens and collected principal seed its open-market pool. The liquidity position is locked, while the creator's fee share remains claimable through its declared recipient split.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:02:03.500
The forest also has a common token. RDAO begins with a disclosed bonding sale and locked-liquidity allocation. Stake it after the twenty-four-hour warm-up to share in WETH rewards, while one token remains one vote. Governance keeps its quorum, proposal threshold, vote, and Timelock visible.

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:23.500
Markets can be volatile. Routes can pause. Smart contracts and chains carry risk. Sherwood does not promise profit, graduation, liquidity, or rewards. It promises rules you can inspect, accounting you can follow, and emergency controls you can see.

00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:33.500
Explore the markets. Plant a token. And see what your community can grow. Devnet demonstration only. These assets and transactions have no real-world value.
